.Sh DESCRIPTION
All of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_bn_param 3
for any methods that return a
.Vt BIGNUM .
Refer to
.Xr EVP_PKEY-DH 7
for more information.
.Pp
An RSA object contains the components for the public and private key,
.Fa n ,
.Fa e ,
.Fa d ,
.Fa p ,
.Fa q ,
.Fa dmp1 ,
.Fa dmq1
and
.Fa iqmp .
.Fa n
is the modulus common to both public and private key,
.Fa e
is the public exponent and
.Fa d
is the private exponent.
.Fa p ,
.Fa q ,
.Fa dmp1 ,
.Fa dmq1
and
.Fa iqmp
are the factors for the second representation of a private key (see
PKCS#1 section 3 Key Types), where
.Fa p
and
.Fa q
are the first and second factor of
.Fa n
and
.Fa dmp1 ,
.Fa dmq1
and
.Fa iqmp
are the exponents and coefficient for CRT calculations.
.Pp
For multi-prime RSA (defined in RFC 8017), there are also one or more
'triplet' in an RSA object.
A triplet contains three members,
.Fa r ,
.Fa d
and
.Sy t .
.Fa r
is the additional prime besides
.Fa p
and
.Fa q .
.Fa d
and
.Sy t
are the exponent and coefficient for CRT calculations.
.Pp
The
.Fa n ,
.Fa e
and
.Fa d
parameters can be obtained by calling
.Fn RSA_get0_key .
If they have not been set yet, then
.Sy *n ,
.Sy *e
and
.Sy *d
will be set to NULL. Otherwise, they are set to pointers to their
respective values.
These point directly to the internal representations of the values and
therefore should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
The
.Fa n ,
.Fa e
and
.Fa d
parameter values can be set by calling
.Fn RSA_set0_key
and passing the new values for
.Fa n ,
.Fa e
and
.Fa d
as parameters to the function.
The values
.Fa n
and
.Fa e
must be non-NULL the first time this function is called on a given RSA
object.
The value
.Fa d
may be NULL. On subsequent calls any of these values may be NULL which
means the corresponding RSA field is left untouched.
Calling this function transfers the memory management of the values to
the RSA object, and therefore the values that have been passed in should
not be freed by the caller after this function has been called.
.Pp
In a similar fashion, the
.Fa p
and
.Fa q
parameters can be obtained and set with
.Fn RSA_get0_factors
and
.Fn RSA_set0_factors ,
and the
.Fa dmp1 ,
.Fa dmq1
and
.Fa iqmp
parameters can be obtained and set with
.Fn RSA_get0_crt_params
and
.Fn RSA_set0_crt_params .
.Pp
For
.Fn RSA_get0_key ,
.Fn RSA_get0_factors ,
and
.Fn RSA_get0_crt_params ,
NULL value BIGNUM ** output parameters are permitted.
The functions ignore NULL parameters but return values for other,
non-NULL, parameters.
.Pp
For multi-prime RSA,
.Fn RSA_get0_multi_prime_factors
and
.Xr RSA_get0_multi_prime_params 3
can be used to obtain other primes and related CRT parameters.
The return values are stored in an array of
.Sy BIGNUM * .
.Fn RSA_set0_multi_prime_params
sets a collect of multi-prime 'triplet' members (prime, exponent and
coefficient) into an RSA object.
.Pp
Any of the values
.Fa n ,
.Fa e ,
.Fa d ,
.Fa p ,
.Fa q ,
.Fa dmp1 ,
.Fa dmq1 ,
and
.Fa iqmp
can also be retrieved separately by the corresponding function
.Fn RSA_get0_n ,
.Fn RSA_get0_e ,
.Fn RSA_get0_d ,
.Fn RSA_get0_p ,
.Fn RSA_get0_q ,
.Fn RSA_get0_dmp1 ,
.Fn RSA_get0_dmq1 ,
and
.Fn RSA_get0_iqmp ,
respectively.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_get0_pss_params
is used to retrieve the RSA-PSS parameters.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_set_flags
sets the flags in the
.Fa flags
parameter on the RSA object.
Multiple flags can be passed in one go (bitwise ORed together).
Any flags that are already set are left set.
.Fn RSA_test_flags
tests to see whether the flags passed in the
.Fa flags
parameter are currently set in the RSA object.
Multiple flags can be tested in one go.
All flags that are currently set are returned, or zero if none of the
flags are set.
.Fn RSA_clear_flags
clears the specified flags within the RSA object.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_get0_engine
returns a handle to the ENGINE that has been set for this RSA object, or
NULL if no such ENGINE has been set.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_get_version
returns the version of an RSA object
.Fa r .
.Sh NOTES
Values retrieved with
.Fn RSA_get0_key
are owned by the RSA object used in the call and may therefore
.Em not
be passed to
.Fn RSA_set0_key .
If needed, duplicate the received value using
.Xr BN_dup 3
and pass the duplicate.
The same applies to
.Fn RSA_get0_factors
and
.Fn RSA_set0_factors
as well as
.Fn RSA_get0_crt_params
and
.Fn RSA_set0_crt_params .
.Pp
The caller should obtain the size by calling
.Fn RSA_get_multi_prime_extra_count
in advance and allocate sufficient buffer to store the return values
before calling
.Fn RSA_get0_multi_prime_factors
and
.Xr RSA_get0_multi_prime_params 3 .
.Pp
.Fn RSA_set0_multi_prime_params
always clears the original multi-prime triplets in RSA object
.Fa r
and assign the new set of triplets into it.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn RSA_set0_key ,
.Fn RSA_set0_factors ,
.Fn RSA_set0_crt_params
and
.Fn RSA_set0_multi_prime_params
return 1 on success or 0 on failure.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_get0_n ,
.Fn RSA_get0_e ,
.Fn RSA_get0_d ,
.Fn RSA_get0_p ,
.Fn RSA_get0_q ,
.Fn RSA_get0_dmp1 ,
.Fn RSA_get0_dmq1 ,
and
.Fn RSA_get0_iqmp
return the respective value.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_get0_pss_params
returns a
.Sy RSA_PSS_PARAMS
pointer, or NULL if there is none.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_get0_multi_prime_factors
and
.Fn RSA_get0_multi_prime_crt_params
return 1 on success or 0 on failure.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_get_multi_prime_extra_count
returns two less than the number of primes in use, which is 0 for
traditional RSA and the number of extra primes for multi-prime RSA.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_get_version
returns
.Sy RSA_ASN1_VERSION_MULTI
for multi-prime RSA and
.Sy RSA_ASN1_VERSION_DEFAULT
for normal two-prime RSA, as defined in RFC 8017.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_test_flags
returns the current state of the flags in the RSA object.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_get0_engine
returns the ENGINE set for the RSA object or NULL if no ENGINE has been
set.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr RSA_new 3 ,
.Xr RSA_size 3
.Sh HISTORY
